findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase distinguished NotFound from other errors in from_file_or_default.
    The config_loading tests exist but none specifically test that parse errors or
    permission errors propagate rather than falling back to defaults.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #2 flags CWE-209: ''ServerError Display leaks internal
    details'' noting reqwest error paths can contain connection details, DNS info,
    internal hostnames. Also notes the security test has a vacuous OR assertion.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote security tests for CRLF injection in tenant IDs (header injection\
    \ risk). Dev implemented CRLF/null-byte validation in SiemClient::new(). However,\
    \ the deeper issue of using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core\
    \ was not flagged \u2014 only the injection vector was mitigated, not the type-safety\
    \ gap."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Reviewer did not mention this Cargo.toml issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #4 explicitly flags: ''ClientConfig silently accepts
    unknown TOML fields... Should use #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] to catch typos.''
    Rated HIGH and blocks merge.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #10 flags the vacuous assertion in security_test.rs:27
    using || instead of &&, noting ''This test can never fail regardless of the Display
    impl. It''s a false-pass bug.'' Though the specific test cited (I5) is about config
    assertions with is_none() || true, the reviewer caught the pattern of vacuous
    OR assertions.'
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. The TEA wrote config tests but this specific vacuously-true
    test pattern was not identified.
